# EDG's OWN C++ runtime -- operator new/delete, vtable support, static
# initialisation, pure-virtual, RTTI -- as C, translated by EDG's own
# C-generating back end.  See sys/src/external/edg/NOTE.
#
# NOT libstdc++ and nothing like it: that is the whole reason this path
# is tractable on a target with no C++ compiler, and it is why this is
# 51 small files rather than a port.
#
# THE ARCHIVE IS WHY THIS GOES FIRST.  The recorded open problem is the
# LINK model -- EDG's COMDAT emulation for vague linkage, with 3,094
# symbols named in more than one of `src''s 75 files -- and an archive
# does not have that problem: `ar' takes duplicate members happily and
# the clash only arrives when something LINKS them.  So this directory
# answers the question nothing has answered yet, "does pcc compile
# EDG's generated C at all", without the link model in the way.
#
# NO -I AND NO -D, deliberately and measured rather than assumed: each
# file here is a WHOLE LOWERED TRANSLATION UNIT and declares everything
# it uses, down to `void *memcpy(void *, const void *, unsigned long
# long)' -- that `unsigned long long' is kencc's own size_t, from
# `kencc_targ.h', so the declarations already describe this target.
# The NOTE records `gcc -fsyntax-only' over all 133 files at 0 errors
# and 0 warnings, which says the sources are clean and says nothing
# about kencc.
#
# CFLAGS WAS `-c' ALONE AND IS `-c -C' NOW, and the reason the first
# spelling existed has expired rather than been overruled: every
# diagnostic was wanted on the first run through pcc, and a flag added
# to quiet one would have hidden the rest.  That run happened -- 50 of
# 51 compile, `c99_complex.c' named by token before it -- so the first
# run is spent.
#
# `-C' IS WHAT THE LINK NEEDS, and the measurement is from the link
# rather than from reading.  An ARCHIVE takes duplicate members
# silently, so building `libedg.a' without it looked clean; the clash
# arrives when `cmd/edg' pulls two members that both define a
# vague-linkage entity.  `6l' answered
#
#	(295) DATA _ZTSv+0(SB)/1,$118
#	__tourite_needs_stdio_exit: multiple initialization
#
# for `_ZTSv', `_ZTIv', `_ZTSDn' and `_ZTIDn' -- the `void' and
# `decltype(nullptr)' type-name strings and type_info objects --
# **each of which `throw.c' and `typeinfo.c' both define**, counted
# rather than guessed.  (The symbol name in that message is stale
# `diag' context and names nothing: read the DATA line above it.)
#
# `6l/asm.c:548' suppresses the diagnostic on `sym->dupok', and
# `6l/obj.c:908' sets that from the AGLOBL's DUPOK bit -- which `-C'
# is the only way to ask for.  `cmd/edg' has carried `-C' since the
# round that found it; **this archive did not, so neither definition
# carried the bit and the suppression could not fire.**  It is a
# property of the Sym, so one side carrying it would have been
# enough, which is why the gap reads as "the flag does not work"
# rather than as a missing flag.
#
# `-J' arrives from pcc itself and is correct here -- EDG emits
# real `sizeof' expressions rather than the 132 baked-in sizes cfront's
# C carried, so kencc computes every layout and conforming layout is
# exactly what the generated code wants.
#
# MEASURED: `mk -k install' COMPILES 50 OF THESE 51 FILES.  The one
# that does not is `c99_complex.c', and it was predicted by name and
# by token before the run:
#
#	<noname>:42[stdin:45] syntax error, last name: _Float16
#
# It is the C99 `_Complex' runtime and builds its own
# `struct _Complex_float16 { _Float16 _Vals[2]; }', `__bf16',
# `__float80' and `__float128' -- gcc's extended floats, none of which
# `cc/lex.c' has ever heard of.  They drag in a whole libgcc soft-float
# family with them (`__addtf3', `__multf3', `__eqhf2',
# `__extendbfsf2', ...) which kencc has not got either, so the file is
# twice out of reach.  COMMENTED OUT of OFILES below now that the
# measurement has been taken, rather than left to fail: cpfe is a C++
# front end and has no use for a `_Complex' runtime, and leaving it in
# makes a plain `mk' stop for a member nothing references.
#
# The corpus was swept for the whole class at once, with comments,
# string and character literals and `#line' stripped FIRST -- and the
# stripping is the measurement rather than a tidying step.  A raw grep
# reports `alignof' 2343 times, `typeof' 425, `static_assert' 1156 and
# `_Complex' 702, and every one of those is ZERO afterwards: they were
# EDG's own diagnostic text and mangled names like
# `_ZN3edg27ec_wrong_entity_for_alignasE', the word inside a longer
# identifier, never a keyword use.
#
# **AND THE SWEEP ALSO NAMED TWO FILES THAT COMPILED FINE, WHICH IS
# THE MORE USEFUL HALF.**  `thread_dtor.c' and `dtor_list.c' use
# `__thread', and I called them against C dialects FROM MEMORY rather
# than against the compiler in this repository -- where
# `cc/lex.c:1765' has carried `"__thread", LNAME, 0' and a swallow at
# `:1095' all along, under the comment *"Plan 9 has no TLS; silently
# drop the qualifier."*  *An instrument whose keyword list is not the
# COMPILER's keyword list is measuring a different compiler*, which is
# the include-path lesson `apdecl-sweep' and `apehdr-sweep' each paid
# for, arriving one level down for a lexer.  The list to check against
# is `cc/lex.c''s `itab' plus that swallow list, and both are in the
# tree; checking the four float types against it afterwards is what
# says `c99_complex.c' really is the only one.
#
# THAT PASS IS NOT A CLEAN BILL, and this is where it will be read.
# `__thread' DROPPED means `__thread_needed_destruction_head' is one
# process-wide global shared by every thread instead of one per thread
# -- this tree's commonest bug shape, a stub answering the wrong thing
# rather than "nothing to do".  Harmless for cpfe, which is
# single-threaded; a live hazard for anything else cpfe ever
# translates.  Recorded, not fixed, and not this mkfile's to fix.
#
# Two things the same sweep CONFIRMED rather than found, and both are
# about the translation having really used this tree:
# `extern unsigned char _ctype[];' appears in nine of `src''s files,
# byte for byte what APE's own <ctype.h> declares -- so the staged
# headers were APExp's and not glibc's, independently of the NOTE
# saying so.  *It also pins this generated C to this tree's `_ctype'
# BIT LAYOUT*, which the `_ISblank' round changed, so a re-translation
# is the price of changing it again.  And `6c/6.out.h''s `NSYM 50' is
# NOT a cap on symbols per object: `swt.c:229' wraps the slot back to 1
# and re-emits the name, so a 315,616-line translation unit costs
# repeated ANAME records rather than hitting a wall.

